Telegram Topic Only — Hermes Agent plugin

By default, keep the root of one Telegram bot DM silent. Commands (including /topic,
/stop and /help), ordinary messages, edits and attachments from the root
are discarded before Hermes dispatch or session recording. Private topics,
including newly created ones, need no registration. Other DMs, groups,
inline button callbacks and inline queries are not filtered. This plugin
does not delete messages from Telegram or change existing Hermes history.

The rule uses the incoming message, not the open Telegram tab. A private
message marked as a topic message with thread ID greater than 1 passes;
missing metadata, reply anchors without a topic flag and General (1) do not.
If sending from All creates a real new topic, or Telegram delivers a reply
from All as belonging to an existing topic, it passes. It is not possible
to reject these while also accepting all legitimate new topics based on the
same metadata.

Optional exceptions: see config.example.yaml for the profile settings. The
root_allowlist defaults to []. Each entry permits exactly one full text (a
slash command or a phrase). Case, whitespace, @bot suffixes and arguments
must match literally: allowing /help does not allow /help anything. List a
specific argument form separately if needed. Captions are not text messages.
A match passes through to normal Hermes processing, including authorization,
routing and history. Restart the gateway after changing the settings.

Deployment (operator action; not needed to run tests):
  1. Enable threaded mode and create a topic before turning on this filter.
  2. In the intended Hermes profile, place plugin.yaml and __init__.py in
     a new plugins/telegram-topic-only/ directory. Do not overwrite an
     existing installation. No additional runtime dependencies are needed
     beyond the Hermes Telegram adapter and its python-telegram-bot package.
  3. Using that profile's CLI, set your private chat ID once (not a topic ID):
       hermes config set plugins.entries.telegram-topic-only.settings.chat_id <CHAT_ID>
  4. Enable with `hermes plugins enable telegram-topic-only` and restart the
     gateway. Verify the plugin loaded: a missing/invalid chat ID prevents
     registration, not gateway startup. Send /status inside a new topic
     (normal response), then as a standalone root message (no response).
     Rollback: `hermes plugins disable telegram-topic-only` and restart.

Offline verification: from this directory run `python -m unittest discover
-s tests -v` using an interpreter with python-telegram-bot 22.6 installed.
Tests exercise real PTB dispatch without contacting Telegram or an LLM.